.TH start-tunnel-port-forward-update-label 1  "update-label "
.SH NAME
start\-tunnel\-port\-forward\-update\-label \- Update the label of a port forward
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstart\-tunnel port\-forward update\-label\fR [\fB\-\-protocol\fR] [\fB\-\-hostname\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISOURCE\fR> [\fILABEL\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Update the label of a port forward
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-protocol\fR \fI<PROTOCOL>\fR [default: tcp]
Transport for hostname routes and fallbacks; plain DNAT forwards use both transports
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
tcp
.IP \(bu 2
udp
.IP \(bu 2
tcp+udp
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-hostname\fR \fI<HOSTNAME>\fR
Selects a hostname; omitted labels this transport’s fallback or a plain forward
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISOURCE\fR>

.TP
[\fILABEL\fR]

